# Test Motion Baselines Across Horizons

Measure when persistence and constant-velocity assumptions stop being competitive.
All experiments use the held-out MABe test file, eight observed frames, seed 42,
and the same sampled windows. Only the prediction horizon changes.

| Config | Observed | Predicted | Future duration |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| `pred12` | 8 frames | 12 frames | 0.4 s |
| `pred30` | 8 frames | 30 frames | 1.0 s |
| `pred60` | 8 frames | 60 frames | 2.0 s |

## Run the benchmark

This cell evaluates persistence, rigid constant velocity, and per-keypoint
constant velocity. It appends one record per baseline to the horizon-specific
JSONL ledger and prints overall and motion-stratified tables.

```python {"interpreter":"/home/splion/Desktop/personal/interpreting-social-navigation/.venv/bin/python"}
import os
from pathlib import Path
import sys

from rich import box
from rich.console import Console
from rich.table import Table

repo_root = next(path for path in [Path.cwd(), *Path.cwd().parents] if (path / "src").exists())
os.environ.setdefault("MPLCONFIGDIR", str(repo_root / "outputs/matplotlib"))
sys.path.insert(0, str(repo_root / "src"))

from evaluate import (
    build_baseline_evaluation_record,
    evaluate_motion_baselines,
    load_motion_baseline_config,
    load_test_config,
    print_motion_stratified_metrics,
    resolve_baseline_window_config,
    save_evaluation_record,
)
from train import load_flat_fit_config

TRAIN_CONFIG = repo_root / "src/config/dense_keypoint__train.yml"
TEST_CONFIG = repo_root / "src/config/test.yml"
BASELINE_CONFIGS = (
    repo_root / "src/config/motion_baselines_pred12__evaluate.yml",
    repo_root / "src/config/motion_baselines_pred30__evaluate.yml",
    repo_root / "src/config/motion_baselines_pred60__evaluate.yml",
)

base_train_config = load_flat_fit_config(TRAIN_CONFIG)
test_config = load_test_config(TEST_CONFIG)
records = []

for baseline_config_path in BASELINE_CONFIGS:
    baseline_config = load_motion_baseline_config(baseline_config_path)
    train_config = resolve_baseline_window_config(base_train_config, baseline_config)
    results = evaluate_motion_baselines(
        train_config=train_config,
        baseline_config=baseline_config,
        split="test",
        test_data_path=test_config.data_path,
        max_windows=baseline_config.max_windows,
        show_progress=True,
    )
    for result in results:
        record = build_baseline_evaluation_record(
            result=result,
            train_config=train_config,
            train_config_path=TRAIN_CONFIG,
            baseline_config=baseline_config,
            baseline_config_path=baseline_config_path,
            split="test",
            test_config_path=TEST_CONFIG,
            test_data_path=test_config.data_path,
            max_windows=baseline_config.max_windows,
            seed=baseline_config.seed,
        )
        save_evaluation_record(record, baseline_config.results_path)
        records.append(record)
        print(f"\n{result.baseline}: prediction={train_config.prediction_length} frames")
        print_motion_stratified_metrics(
            metrics_by_motion=result.metrics_by_motion,
            motion_profile=result.motion_profile,
        )

table = Table(title="Motion-baseline difficulty curve", box=box.SIMPLE_HEAVY)
for column in ("horizon", "baseline", "cADE px", "cFDE px", "DME px", "DG", "seconds"):
    table.add_column(column, justify="right" if column != "baseline" else "left")
for record in records:
    metrics = record["metrics"]
    table.add_row(
        str(record["model"]["prediction_length"]),
        record["model"]["baseline"],
        f'{metrics["centroid_ade_px"]:.3f}',
        f'{metrics["centroid_fde_px"]:.3f}',
        f'{metrics["displacement_magnitude_error_px"]:.3f}',
        f'{metrics["displacement_gain"]:.3f}',
        f'{record["runtime_seconds"]:.2f}',
    )
Console().print(table)
```

## CLI equivalents

Run one horizon independently when iterating:

```sh
python src/evaluate.py --config src/config/dense_keypoint__train.yml --test-config src/config/test.yml --baseline-config src/config/motion_baselines_pred12__evaluate.yml --split test
python src/evaluate.py --config src/config/dense_keypoint__train.yml --test-config src/config/test.yml --baseline-config src/config/motion_baselines_pred30__evaluate.yml --split test
python src/evaluate.py --config src/config/dense_keypoint__train.yml --test-config src/config/test.yml --baseline-config src/config/motion_baselines_pred60__evaluate.yml --split test
```

Results are stored separately under
`outputs/evaluations/motion_baselines/pred{12,30,60}/results.jsonl`.

## Recorded 1,000-window results

The aligned held-out run produced the following aggregate values. Lower is
better for the error columns; displacement gain is best at 1.0.

| Horizon | Baseline | cADE px | cFDE px | kADE px | kFDE px | DME px | DG |
| ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 12 | persistence | 6.484 | 10.886 | 8.154 | 13.335 | 10.886 | 0.000 |
| 12 | rigid constant velocity | 6.467 | 11.788 | 8.232 | 14.223 | 8.289 | 1.728 |
| 12 | keypoint constant velocity | 6.467 | 11.788 | 9.789 | 17.378 | 8.289 | 1.728 |
| 30 | persistence | 13.228 | 23.543 | 15.835 | 27.281 | 23.543 | 0.000 |
| 30 | rigid constant velocity | 16.139 | 32.615 | 18.514 | 35.480 | 24.711 | 2.900 |
| 30 | keypoint constant velocity | 16.139 | 32.615 | 22.790 | 44.196 | 24.711 | 2.900 |
| 60 | persistence | 23.182 | 41.378 | 26.655 | 46.186 | 41.378 | 0.000 |
| 60 | rigid constant velocity | 33.872 | 69.235 | 36.611 | 72.451 | 52.644 | 4.607 |
| 60 | keypoint constant velocity | 33.872 | 69.235 | 45.473 | 90.566 | 52.644 | 4.607 |

Persistence cFDE by ground-truth motion stratum makes the aggregate result more
interpretable:

| Horizon | Low motion | Medium motion | High motion |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 12 | 1.354 px | 4.585 px | 26.748 px |
| 30 | 1.935 px | 8.431 px | 60.327 px |
| 60 | 2.592 px | 15.550 px | 106.108 px |

## Interpretation

- Persistence predicts zero displacement, so its displacement gain is zero.
- Displacement direction is undefined for persistence because a zero vector has
  no direction; DME and displacement gain capture this failure.
- Compare models within each horizon and motion stratum. Increasing errors with
  horizon establish a difficulty curve; aggregate errors alone can hide failure
  on high-motion windows.
- Do not remove low-motion windows. The strata diagnose the distribution without
  redefining valid mouse behavior.
